Parity disposition (faithful, no scope narrowing):
  - Web <MaskedValue> is a PURE presentational primitive (no fetch / React-Query / Promise) -> it has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch. Inventing such chrome would FABRICATE states the source does not have, so this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches, exactly as the sibling presentational primitives StatusHero (0199) and CopyButton (0207) did. The real branches are:
       * empty    (raw.length === 0) -> em-dash in the muted tone with the caller aria-label, NO toggle (web early return).
       * masked   (default)          -> variant-masked bullets in the secondary tone + eye toggle (+ optional copy).
       * revealed                    -> cleartext in the accent tone + eye-off toggle; auto-hides after autoHideMs (default 30000ms).
    x 5 masking variants (token / vin / coords / email / generic), each a byte-for-byte port of maskFor's per-variant rule from web/src/lib/maskValue.ts (verified by AdapterTests with independently-built bullet expectations).
  - side effects faithfully reproduced via seams (no direct HTTP from the view):
       * reveal-audit (web fire-and-forget POST /audit/reveal {kind:'masked_reveal', variant}) -> injected MaskedValueAuditRecorder; fires ONLY when auditOnReveal=true (web default false, preserved); default OSLog recorder is non-network + never-throwing (errors swallowed by design, web parity). MaskedValueAudit.kind == "masked_reveal".
       * auto-hide  (web setTimeout/clearTimeout) -> a cancellable Task armed on reveal, cancelled on hide/toggle/update-to-empty/stop (web unmount clearTimer); reset-to-masked on teardown so a re-appear shows the masked form (web remount).
       * copy       (web <CopyButton text iconOnly ariaLabel> always copies the RAW value) -> the shared CopyButton surface (0207), keyed on the raw value so a changed secret rebuilds it with fresh copy text.
  - i18n: the web resolves three labels via t() (mask.reveal/'Reveal value', mask.hide/'Hide value', mask.copy/'Copy value'); native ships NO English literals, so those are lifted into the P1/S10 "MaskedValue" table and resolved through MaskedValueStrings. value + ariaLabel are caller-supplied (already-localized) and rendered verbatim.
  - a11y: the raw secret is NEVER the VoiceOver LABEL (the semantic ariaLabel is, web aria-label parity); the cleartext is exposed only as the accessibility VALUE once revealed (a user who explicitly revealed can still hear it). Toggle carries the state-mirrored label + .isSelected (web aria-pressed); decorative glyphs hidden; container carries accessibilityIdentifier (web data-testid). Dynamic Type via the relative .callout monospaced style; no motion added (web has none) so Reduce Motion is inherently respected.
  - tokens: Color.TS.accent / textSecondary / textMuted, Font/.system(.callout, .monospaced), TSSpacing, TSButton, CopyButton — NO Tailwind ports, no raw hex. The cyan-300 reveal hue maps to the theme-aware Color.TS.accent (same fixed-hue->token rationale as StatusHero).

